{"id": "EUVD-2026-81826", "enisaUuid": "67dabdb3-c0ba-3e92-8dfe-7760959779c8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnvme-pci: release descriptor pools on probe failure\n\nThe per-NUMA-node descriptor DMA pools are created lazily from\nnvme_init_hctx_common() once the admin tag set is allocated, but they are\nonly destroyed in nvme_remove() via nvme_release_descriptor_pools(). Any\nprobe failure after the admin tag set has been allocated unwinds through\nthe out_disable label and nvme_pci_free_ctrl(), neither of which releases\nthe pools, leaking the dma_pool objects.\n\nRelease the descriptor pools in the out_disable error path. It must not\nbe added to nvme_pci_free_ctrl(), as that would double-free against\nnvme_remove() on the normal teardown path.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:00:09", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c25b6b28a35f9e36ce5dd6da5905bcddb2128707", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/79fb405966edb5065234440d94cc75bfd7b01f41", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cb144c2f67128abfa5c7ba33318617d19f192156"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90233", "GHSA-jqrr-g5gr-9xjv"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2cb536d2-c3d4-308f-b313-ea77c4e9c552", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d977506f8863807129d7a11f4057dfb1b38085ea <79fb405966edb5065234440d94cc75bfd7b01f41"}, {"id": "46aa3d79-71bc-3743-80d4-88dc12afc346", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "5d63b41b-8fa7-30b5-94d4-dcd59814c36d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "8f545ffd-0c0d-3f74-be3b-ebeb9cab8480", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d977506f8863807129d7a11f4057dfb1b38085ea <cb144c2f67128abfa5c7ba33318617d19f192156"}, {"id": "ab21fb41-6b2f-3dbe-bdfc-740c1421a632", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.16"}, {"id": "dc5ffc26-d8a0-3efb-9a2b-f1dd167ea7a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "ea407428-d3df-3904-9835-5334c306d937", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d977506f8863807129d7a11f4057dfb1b38085ea <c25b6b28a35f9e36ce5dd6da5905bcddb2128707"}, {"id": "f6bfcdcc-49f0-3052-a340-e8a8f62a1232", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f61eda09-ded6-36c3-8dfe-0dd0a691b5ca", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}